WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.620
1, 3, minus 5 and 8.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.960
This is just a row of four numbers

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.980
and this can be represented in different ways.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.360
We can write it as an array of numbers horizontally like this

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.280
or we can write it as an array of numbers vertically like this.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.480
The first part as you can see has one row and four columns

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.000
and the second part has four rows and one column.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.580
There's another way in which we can write the four numbers.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.640
The first two numbers in the first row

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.540
and the last two numbers in the second row.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.540
All these three things you see here are called matrices.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.180
Each of these is a Matrix.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.560
Just an arrangement of rows and columns.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.680
But how do we properly define it?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.760
We can say that a matrix is a rectangular arrangement.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.680
But a rectangular arrangement of what?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.200
It can be anything.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.380
Numbers, letters or the characters. Anything.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.300
A Matrix is made up of rows and column.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.920
The first Matrix has one row and four columns.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.060
The second one has four rows and one column.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.000
And what about the third one?

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.500
It has two rows and 2 columns.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.120
So a matrix is just a rectangular arrangement of rows and columns

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.040
But there is one important condition we need to keep in mind.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.700
Each row needs to have equal number of elements.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.890
For instance in the second Matrix,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.120
each row has one element.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.920
And in the third matrix each row has two elements.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.160
And each column also needs to have equal number of elements.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.920
In the first Matrix each column has one element,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.620
the second Matrix has just one column so it doesn't matter

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.020
and in the third one each column has two elements.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.639
So a matrix is a

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.380
rectangular arrangement of rows and columns

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.180
in which each row has equal number of elements

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.000
and each column as well has equal number of elements.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.920
So is this a Matrix?

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.080
Elements 'a' and 'b' in the first row

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.580
and elements 'c' and 'd' in the second.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.040
It is a rectangular arrangement.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.920
Each row has two elements

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.860
and each column has two elements.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.660
It is a Matrix!

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.540
And these three are also Matrices.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.160
Okay, what about this one with three elements?

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.680
Is it a matrix?

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.480
The first row has two elements

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.140
but the second one has just has one element.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.180
So it is not a matrix.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.840
What about this one with five elements?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.300
The number of elements in each of the columns

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.570
is not the same.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:42.660
It's 2, 1 and 2 and this as well is not a matrix.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.700
So this is the definition.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.680
A rectangular arrangement of rows and columns in

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.599
which each row should have equal number of elements

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:52.060
and each column as well.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.320
should have equal number of elements.

